# ========================================
# Gateway Global AI Platform - Environment Configuration
# ========================================
# This file contains all environment variables needed for the platform.
# Copy this file to .env (or .env.local) and replace placeholder values with your actual credentials.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit .env, .env.local, or env.local to version control!
#
# For setup help, see: https://github.com/gateway-global-ai/chat-mvp-merge/blob/main/README.md
# For storing and sharing secrets across dev/stage/prod, see: docs/deployment/SECRETS_AND_ENV.md
# ========================================

# ========================================
# DOPPLER (secret management — do not commit .env)
# ========================================
# IMPORTANT: Spelling is DOPPLER (two P's). Use DOPPLER_TOKEN or DOPPLER_TOKEN_DEV —
# NOT DOPLER_TOKEN or DOPPLER_DEV_TOKEN. The Doppler CLI only reads DOPPLER_TOKEN.
#
# Canonical token names (aligned with .cursor/rules/doppler-cli.mdc and Doppler configs dev/stg/prd):
#
#   DOPPLER_TOKEN_DEV   — Token for Doppler config "dev" (dev server, port 3004)
#   DOPPLER_TOKEN_STG   — Token for Doppler config "stg" (stage server, port 3003)
#   DOPPLER_TOKEN_PRD   — Token for Doppler config "prd" (prod server, port 3002)
#
# The Doppler CLI reads DOPPLER_TOKEN only — not DOPPLER_DEV_PERSONAL_TOKEN or other custom names.
# Put your service account token (dp.sa…) or service token (dp.st…) in DOPPLER_TOKEN, or export DOPPLER_TOKEN from .env before doppler run.
#
# The Doppler CLI reads DOPPLER_TOKEN. On each server, set the token for that environment:
# - Either set DOPPLER_TOKEN (used by doppler run and scripts), or
# - Set only the labeled var (e.g. DOPPLER_TOKEN_DEV on dev); scripts fall back to it when DOPPLER_TOKEN is unset.
#
# DOPPLER_TOKEN_DEV=dp.st.dev.xxxx
# DOPPLER_TOKEN_STG=dp.st.stg.xxxx
# DOPPLER_TOKEN_PRD=dp.st.prd.xxxx
# Or for the current server only:
# DOPPLER_TOKEN=dp.st.xxxx
#
# Ports: each Doppler config has PORT. PORT_DEV, PORT_STG, PORT_PRD prevent overwrite when pushing env. Run "npm run doppler:sync-ports" to set PORT in each config.
# PORT_DEV=3004
# PORT_STG=3003
# PORT_PRD=3002
#
# Optional: DOPPLER_EXPECT_ENV=dev|stg|prod — used by GET /api/health to verify DOPPLER_TOKEN matches this environment (detects wrong-token copy). Do not store token vars in Doppler; keep them only in .env on each server.
# DOPPLER_EXPECT_ENV=dev

# ========================================
# DATABASE
# ========================================
# PostgreSQL database connection string
# Format: postgresql://username:password@host:port/database
# 
# Local development example:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/gateway_ai
#
# Production (use connection pooling):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@db.example.com:5432/gateway_ai?sslmode=require&pool_timeout=10

# ========================================
# AI SERVICES
# ========================================


# ========================================
# CLOUDBEDS (PMS — hospitality; optional)
# ========================================
# Per-site credentials live in site_pms_integrations; these support OAuth + global API key fallback.
# CLOUDBEDS_API_BASE_URL=https://api.cloudbeds.com/api/v1.3
# CLOUDBEDS_OAUTH_AUTHORIZE_URL=https://api.cloudbeds.com/api/v1.3/oauth/authorize
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_ID=live1_...
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_CALLBACK_URL=https://your-public-host/api/cloudbeds/oauth/callback
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_API_KEY=cbat_...
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_PROPERTY_ID=315701
# Legacy aliases: CLOUDBEDS_API_KEY, CLOUDBEDS_PROPERTY_ID

# Google Gemini (AI Studio / Generative Language API) — canonical name used by server
# Get your API key from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Used for: Gemini Live voice, LLM reasoning, grounded responses (see docs/API_KEYS_DOPPLER.md)
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Google API key — general fallback for Maps/Places/other Google APIs (non-Gemini)
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_google_api_key_here



# ========================================
# GOOGLE CLOUD PLATFORM
# ========================================

# Server-side Maps/Places: ONE key for both Maps Grounding Lite and Places API (New).
# Using different keys for Grounding Lite vs Places API (New) causes pull failures; they must be the same.
# Client-side keys (GOOGLE_MAPS_JS_API, etc.) can be different; server-side must be a single key.
# Set one of these (code checks in order): GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY, GOOGLE_MAPS_GROUNDING_LITE_API_KEY, GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY
# Enable Maps Grounding Lite API + Places API (New) on the same key in GCP: https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=your_google_maps_api_key_here

# Alternative name — same key value as above (do not set a different key here)
# GOOGLE_MAPS_GROUNDING_LITE_API_KEY=same_key_as_above

# Optional alias — same key value (do not use a different key for Places vs Grounding Lite)
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=your_google_places_api_key_here

# Google Cloud Project ID
# Find at: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# Used for: Server-side Google API calls (general app)
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id

# Google Cloud API key (server-side Maps/Places/Cloud); code also uses getServerMapsApiKey() fallback chain above
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_API_KEY=your_google_cloud_api_key_here

# Client Maps JS key — served via /api/config/maps-key or build; code reads GOOGLE_MAPS_JS_API or GOOGLE_MAPS_JS_KEY
# GOOGLE_MAPS_JS_API=your_maps_js_key_here

# GRN Travel Agent – use this project for all GRN-related Google access (Places, Maps, hotel flows).
# The project was originally grn-travel-agent; GRN features must use this GCP project.
# GRN_GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT_ID=grn-travel-agent

# Google OAuth2 - For Google Workspace Integration
# Create credentials at: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Application type: Web application
# Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:5000/auth/google/callback (dev)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_oauth_client_id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_oauth_client_secret
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5000/auth/google/callback

# Programmatic platform email (Gmail API + Domain-Wide Delegation)
# See docs/integrations/PLATFORM_EMAIL_SERVICE_ACCOUNT.md for one-time setup.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON: MUST be the full JSON content from GCP (the entire key file).
#   Do NOT use the UI key fingerprint or key ID — only the complete JSON object (type, project_id, private_key_id, private_key, client_email, ...).
#   Store in Doppler; paste from e.g. cat ai-biz-bot-emailer-key.json in Cloud Shell.
# PLATFORM_SENDER_EMAIL: Address to send as (DWD subject), e.g. agent@gatewayglobal.ai.
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
PLATFORM_SENDER_EMAIL=

# ========================================
# TWILIO - TELEPHONY & SMS
# ========================================
# Get credentials from: https://console.twilio.com/
# Used for: SMS, voice calls, phone numbers, A2P 10-DLC

# Twilio Account SID (Account identifier)
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your_twilio_account_sid

# Twilio Auth Token (Keep secret!)
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_twilio_auth_token

# Twilio Phone Number (E.164 format: +1234567890). Code also accepts TWILIO_ACCOUNT_PHONE_NUMBER, TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER_BOT.
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=your_twilio_phone_number

# System-level Twilio primary account credentials (preferred)
SYSTEM_TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your_system_twilio_account_sid
SYSTEM_TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your_system_twilio_auth_token
SYSTEM_TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=your_system_twilio_phone_number

# Optional: Twilio API Key (for sub-accounts)
# TWILIO_API_KEY=your_twilio_api_key
# TWILIO_API_SECRET=your_twilio_api_secret

# Verification gate (HTTP): fingerprint pepper (recommended in production; rotate = new hash generation)
# CLIENT_FINGERPRINT_PEPPER=
# Max requests per 60s window per fingerprint bucket; without Redis this is per Node process (per replica)
# VERIFICATION_GATE_MAX_PER_WINDOW=120
# Optional: Redis URL for global rate limits across all app instances (INCR+EXPIRE fixed 60s window)
# VERIFICATION_GATE_REDIS_URL=

# ========================================
# STRIPE - PAYMENT PROCESSING
# ========================================
# Get keys from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
# Used for: Subscriptions, payments, billing

# Stripe Secret Key (server-side, keep secret!)
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=your_stripe_secret_key

# Stripe Publishable Key (client-side, safe to expose)
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_stripe_publishable_key

# Stripe Webhook Secret (for webhook verification)
# Get from: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=your_stripe_webhook_secret

# A2P / Telephony Stripe webhook (optional)
# STRIPE_A2P_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_xxxx

# Stripe Subscription Plan Price IDs — sync from dev to stg/prd via Doppler copy
# STRIPE_PRICE_FREE=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_STARTER=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_ENTERPRISE=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_AI_PRO=price_xxx
# STRIPE_PRICE_AI_BASIC=price_xxx

# Site Claim Activation — one-time $49.99 activation fee for assigned websites
# STRIPE_PRICE_CLAIM_ACTIVATION=price_...

# Partner Energy: one-time refill Price IDs
# STRIPE_PRICE_ENERGY_500=price_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_ENERGY_1200=price_...

# ========================================
# APPLICATION CONFIGURATION
# ========================================

# Node Environment (development | staging | production)
NODE_ENV=development

# Server Port (use 3004 for aibizbot-dev.gatewayglobal.ai standard)
PORT=5000

# Server Host (use 0.0.0.0 to listen on all interfaces when behind a reverse proxy)
HOST=localhost

# WebSocket Port (for real-time features)
WS_PORT=3001

# Application URLs
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5000
SERVER_URL=http://localhost:5000
API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
# Public app URL for Stripe success/cancel, reseller payouts, magic links, QR codes.
# Dev: http://localhost:5000
# Production (www.gatewayglobal.ai at 72.61.4.44): https://www.gatewayglobal.ai
APP_URL=http://localhost:5000

# ========================================
# NOVA SOVEREIGN (IDV / Billing)
# ========================================
# RSA-4096 public key (PEM) for verifying X-Nova-Signature on /api/nova/billing/*.
# Store in Doppler for dev: doppler secrets set NOVA_RSA_PUBLIC_KEY="$(cat path/to/nova_public.pem)"
# Without this key, signed Nova endpoints return 503.
NOVA_RSA_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ========================================
# SECURITY
# ========================================

# Session Secret (REQUIRED - minimum 32 characters)
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
SESSION_SECRET=your_random_session_secret_here_minimum_32_characters

# Encryption Key (REQUIRED for sensitive data - minimum 32 characters)
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_encryption_key_here_minimum_32_characters

# CORS Origins (comma-separated list)
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5000,https://yourdomain.com

# ========================================
# OPTIONAL: EMAIL CONFIGURATION
# ========================================
# For sending transactional emails (notifications, reports, etc.)
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=your_email@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASS=your_email_app_password
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@gateway-global.ai

# ========================================
# OPTIONAL: REDIS (SESSION STORAGE)
# ========================================
# For production session management and caching
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
# REDIS_PASSWORD=your_redis_password
# REDIS_TLS=false

# ========================================
# OPTIONAL: MONITORING & ANALYTICS
# ========================================
# Sentry (Error Tracking)
# SENTRY_DSN=your_sentry_dsn
# SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=development

# Google Analytics
# GA_TRACKING_ID=UA-XXXXXXXXX-X

# PostHog (Product Analytics)
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=your_posthog_key
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com

# ========================================
# FEATURE FLAGS
# ========================================
# Enable/disable platform features (true | false)

# Voice AI Features (Gemini Native Audio)
ENABLE_VOICE_AI=true

# Google Workspace Integration
ENABLE_GOOGLE_WORKSPACE=true

# A2P 10-DLC Compliance Features
ENABLE_A2P_COMPLIANCE=true

# VoiceLeadMachine (Outbound Campaigns)
ENABLE_VOICE_LEAD_MACHINE=true

# Chat Interface Modes
ENABLE_CHAT_FLOAT_MODE=true
ENABLE_CHAT_EXPAND_MODE=true

# ========================================
# LOGGING & DEBUGGING
# ========================================
# Log Level (error | warn | info | debug | trace)
LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Debug Mode (enables verbose logging)
DEBUG=false

# Log to File (optional)
# LOG_FILE=./logs/app.log
# LOG_MAX_SIZE=10m
# LOG_MAX_FILES=7

# ========================================
# RATE LIMITING
# ========================================
# Prevent abuse and ensure fair usage

# Rate limit window (milliseconds) - default 15 minutes
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=900000

# Max requests per window per IP
RATE_LIMIT_MAX_REQUESTS=100

# API rate limits (requests per minute)
# API_RATE_LIMIT_RPM=60

# ========================================
# ADVANCED CONFIGURATION
# ========================================

# Database Connection Pool
# DB_POOL_MIN=2
# DB_POOL_MAX=10
# DB_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# API Timeouts (milliseconds)
# API_TIMEOUT=30000
# AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=120000

# File Upload Limits
# MAX_FILE_SIZE=10485760
# MAX_FILES=10

# ========================================
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY
# ========================================
# These variables are only used in development

# Vite Development Server
# VITE_PORT=5173

# Skip SSL Certificate Validation (NEVER in production!)
# NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0

# Mock API Responses (for testing without external services)
# MOCK_AI_RESPONSES=false
# For initial testing: set to true to avoid sending real SMS
MOCK_TWILIO_SMS=true
# MOCK_STRIPE_PAYMENTS=false

# ========================================
# GEMINI MODEL CONFIG (optional overrides)
# ========================================
# Code defaults: GEMINI_MODEL_ID for native audio/live; GEMINI_MODEL / GEMINI_MODEL_FALLBACK for B2B.
# GEMINI_MODEL_ID=models/gemini-2.5-flash-native-audio-preview-12-2025
# GEMINI_WS_URL= (optional; default: wss://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/ws/...BidiGenerateContent)
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.0-flash
# GEMINI_MODEL_FALLBACK=gemini-2.5-flash

# ========================================
# CLIENT (Vite) — must prefix with VITE_; exposed to browser
# ========================================
# Backend URL for telephony/provisioning (e.g. http://localhost:5000)
# VITE_TELEPHONY_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
# Google Map IDs (Map Tiles API)
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAP_ID=your_map_id
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAP_ID_MIDNIGHT=your_midnight_map_id
# Client-side Maps API key (referrer-restricted in GCP)
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=your_client_maps_key

# ========================================
# B2B TRAVEL OS (Gateway Global)
# ========================================
# SerpAPI - Flights/Maps/Local search (B2B transactional loop + Cursor MCP)
# Canonical: SERP_API_KEY; code also accepts SERPAPI_API_KEY, SERPAPI_KEY.
# Store in Doppler: doppler secrets set SERP_API_KEY="your-key"
# Then generate .cursor/mcp.json: npm run mcp:generate
SERP_API_KEY=your_serp_api_key

# GRN Connect - Hotel/grounding for B2B
# GRN_API_KEY=your_grn_api_key

# Nuitée - Hotel content for B2B
# NUITEE_API_KEY=your_nuitee_api_key

# ========================================
# SETUP NOTES
# ========================================
#
# 1. REQUIRED SERVICES FOR MVP:
#    - PostgreSQL database
#    - Gemini API key (GEMINI_API_KEY — sole AI engine)
#    - Twilio account (SMS/voice)
#    - Stripe account (payments)
#    - Google Cloud Platform project (Maps/Places/Workspace)
#
# 2. OPTIONAL BUT RECOMMENDED:
#    - Redis (production session storage)
#    - Sentry (error tracking)
#
# 3. SECURITY CHECKLIST:
#    - [ ] Generate strong SESSION_SECRET (32+ chars)
#    - [ ] Generate strong ENCRYPTION_KEY (32+ chars)
#    - [ ] Use environment-specific values (dev/staging/prod)
#    - [ ] Never commit .env to version control
#    - [ ] Restrict API key permissions to minimum required
#    - [ ] Enable 2FA on all service accounts
#    - [ ] Rotate secrets regularly
#
# 4. GOOGLE CLOUD SETUP:
#    - Enable APIs: Maps JavaScript API, Places API (New), Drive API, 
#      Calendar API, Tasks API, Docs API, Sheets API
#    - Create OAuth 2.0 credentials (Web application)
#    - Add authorized redirect URIs
#    - Set up billing (required for production quotas)
#
# 5. TWILIO SETUP:
#    - Create account at twilio.com
#    - Verify your phone number
#    - Purchase a phone number
#    - Configure A2P 10-DLC registration (for production SMS)
#    - Set up webhook URLs for SMS/Voice
#
# 6. STRIPE SETUP:
#    - Create account at stripe.com
#    - Get API keys (test mode for development)
#    - Configure webhook endpoint
#    - Set up products and pricing
#    - Complete business verification (for production)
#
# For detailed setup instructions, see README.md
# For troubleshooting, see docs/SETUP_GUIDE.md
#
# ========================================
